nodes.body:
@mickqian @BBuf This is now ready for initial review and synced with main at 6fc8d9d. The 85 focused pi0.5 tests passed again after the merge. On Ascend, fixed-noise HTTP comparisons passed for TP=1 and TP=2, including actual continuations; a 12-request staggered-arrival check with varied prompt lengths also passed. Numerical tolerances and limitations are recorded in the PR description.

Could you help review the scheduler/worker integration and authorize the appropriate CI jobs (including the run-ci label and relevant Diffusion/CUDA coverage)? CUDA and the full upstream hardware suite remain unvalidated. The opt-in path is disabled by default; remaining-work bucketing is outside this PR. Related design discussion: #43522.

Thank you.

